   - For oversampling by 16 (`OVER8 = 0` in `USART_CR1` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1740]), the baud rate register value is calculated as [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1708]:
     $$\text{USARTDIV} = \frac{f_{\text{CK}}}{\text{Baud}} = \frac{85\,000\,000}{115\,200} \approx 737.847$$
   - Rounding to the nearest integer yields `BRR = 738` (`0x02E2`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1708, 1755].
   - Resulting baud rate:
     $$\text{Baud}_{\text{actual}} = \frac{85\,000\,000}{738} \approx 115\,176.15\text{ baud}$$
